# Line-ending policy - added Day 18.
#
# THE PROBLEM IT FIXES
#   Every commit was rewriting every file in results/ - 439 insertions and
#   439 deletions with no content change. `git diff -w` (whitespace-blind)
#   showed nothing at all: it was pure CRLF/LF churn from editing on Windows
#   against files written with LF.
#
#   That is not cosmetic. A diff full of phantom changes is a diff nobody
#   reads, which is how a real change to an eval result gets waved through.
#   Results files are evidence; their history has to be legible.
#
# THE POLICY
#   Normalise text to LF in the repository, check out natively on Windows.
* text=auto

# Data and results: LF in the repo and in the working copy, always.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
